# Frontend context graph

Before editing or creating a file under `frontend/`, from the `frontend/` directory run:

```bash
npm run context -- src/components/example.tsx
```

Use the path you are about to change. Follow every decision in that output. Treat rules marked `needs review` as binding until a person clears them in `frontend/context/decisions.yaml`. Use only the tokens the output lists.

- Reuse a component already named in the graph before creating a new one.
- After the edit, run `npm run context:build` and fix any new entries in `frontend/context/violations.json`.
- When a conversation settles a design decision, add it to `frontend/context/decisions.yaml` (`id`, `title`, `rule`, `rationale`, `applies_to`, `needs_review`). Do not leave it only in chat history.

```tsx
// Bad: palette color and an arbitrary type size
<p className="text-red-600 text-[10px]">Overdue</p>

// Good: theme tokens
<p className="text-status-failed text-xs">Overdue</p>
```
